"message": "Guidelines require serum creatinine and eGFR monitoring for patients initiating TDF, and list chronic kidney disease and Fanconi syndrome as TDF toxicities. Patient's creatinine rose from 0.8 to 1.1 mg/dL and eGFR declined to 78 mL/min/1.73m² after 10 weeks on TDF. This upward creatinine trend warrants attention even though the absolute value remains near-normal. DTG and pregnancy also contribute. Evidence for drug attribution: TDF is nephrotoxic and the rise is temporally associated with initiation. Evidence against: pregnancy itself can affect renal parameters, and eGFR of 78 may reflect normal physiologic adaptation. Urinalysis is normal with no protein or glucose, arguing against significant tubular damage.",
"recommended_action": "Repeat serum creatinine and eGFR at next visit. If creatinine continues rising or eGFR declines further, evaluate for TDF toxicity and consider renal-safe alternatives.",
